# ============================================================ Medical
'ems-allergic-reaction' = 'It was in the sauce. I asked them twice and they said there were no nuts in it. | My throat is closing. This is not a cold, I know what this is. | I have a pen for it. It is in my bag. Right hand pocket.'
'ems-anaphylaxis-child' = 'It is my son. He is four years old and he ate it at the table. | I did not know there was any in it. I would never have given him any. | I used the pen. It is the small one, the one they give you for children.'
'ems-assault-victim' = 'Two of them. It came out of nowhere. | I did not get a proper look. Baseball cap, dark jacket, that is all. | Which way did they go? Tell me which way they went.'
'ems-birth' = 'It started on the way here and it has not stopped since. | Two minutes apart. I have been counting them. | I am not going anywhere. This is happening now, in this room.'
'ems-broken-ankle' = 'It has been like this for an hour. I have not moved an inch. | I heard it go. There is no way I am walking down on it. | How are you getting me off this hill? Do not say by stretcher, because that is a joke.'
'ems-burn-injury' = 'It was the pan. It came off the stove and straight over my arm. | Somebody put cold water on it and then somebody else said not to. | It is the fingers. That is the part that will not stop.'
'ems-burns-face' = 'The gas ring. It caught the moment I went to light it. | I turned away, but I was not quick enough. | Just tell me it is not my eyes. Somebody tell me it is not my eyes.'
'ems-carbon-monoxide' = 'It is the boiler. It has been making that noise for weeks. | We all went sleepy, one after the other. All of us. | The children are outside. I put them outside before I called you.'
'ems-chemical-inhalation' = 'One breath. One breath and it went straight into my chest. | Nobody told us what was in the drum. Nobody knows what was in the drum. | I am not going back in there. Do not ask me to go back in there.'
'ems-chest-pain' = 'It came on in the street. I sat down on the first bench I could find. | I have had one before. This is not that one. It is different. | Do not let me walk to the ambulance. I know what walking does.'
'ems-child-drowning' = 'She was under for a while. I do not know how long. | I pulled her out myself and I did the breaths, the ones they show you. | She coughed. That was the sound I wanted. That was the sound.'
'ems-choking' = 'It was a piece of steak. It went down the wrong way. | I put my hands up and somebody did the thing. Somebody did it properly. | I have never been that frightened. That is not an exaggeration.'
'ems-cyclist-down' = 'The door opened in front of me. I had nowhere left to go. | My wrist went under me, but the arm is the problem, not the wrist. | Nobody got the number. Do not ask me for the number.'
'ems-dehydration' = 'It was a half marathon. I have done the distance plenty of times. | I stopped sweating about four miles back. That is when it went wrong. | Water. Not a bottle. All of it.'
'ems-diabetic' = 'I have not eaten since yesterday. It slipped my mind completely. | My hands are shaking and I cannot get a thought to stay still. | Sugar. Anything with sugar in it. Orange juice if anybody has one.'
'ems-dialysis-missed' = 'The transport did not come. It did not come and I could not get there on my own. | I can barely stand up. My legs are like paper. | Do not touch this arm. That is the fistula. Do not touch this arm.'
'ems-dog-bite' = 'It was off the lead. It came from behind the gate. | The owner called it off and then just walked away. She said it had never done that. | It is the bleeding I cannot stop looking at.'
'ems-domestic-injury' = 'It is the door. I walked into the door. | He has gone. He took the car and he has gone. | If you write it down, he will see it written down. Do you understand what I am saying?'
'ems-drowning' = 'The current took me sideways. I could not get back in. | Somebody went in after me. I want to know who it was. | I saw the light on the water and then I saw nothing for a while.'
'ems-elderly-confusion' = 'I was looking for the bus. I know this street. I do not know this street. | Something has not been right all evening. | Is it Wednesday? It cannot be Wednesday.'
'ems-electric-shock' = 'The breaker was supposed to be locked off. It was not locked off. | It threw me back about six feet. I remember the bang. | My hand will not stop. It is still going through me.'
'ems-exposure' = 'The fog came down and the path went with it. | I sat behind a wall for a while. That made it worse, not better. | I cannot get warm. I have been shaking for an hour and I cannot get warm.'
'ems-fall-elderly' = 'I went down in the hallway and I have been here since. | The key is under the plant pot. The neighbour will show you. | Do not lift me by the arms. Please do not lift me by the arms.'
'ems-fall-from-height' = 'Third rung. It was not even the top of the ladder. | I had a box of tiles in one hand. That is why I went. | It is my back. Everything else is fine, it is my back.'
'ems-farm-machinery' = 'It was the power take-off. It caught the sleeve and it pulled. | Do not touch the tractor. It is still in gear. | Nobody switches it off except me. That is the rule on this farm.'
'ems-food-poisoning' = 'It is the buffet. Everybody who had the buffet is like this. | Nine of them now. Three went home before we thought to call you. | It is still out on the table. Nobody has touched it since.'
'ems-forklift' = 'He came round the corner and I had nowhere to step. | It was slow. That is the part people will not believe, it was slow. | Do not tell me what it looked like. I do not want to know what it looked like.'
'ems-glass-assault' = 'It was a glass. He used a glass. | It was the neck, they said. They said it went in at the neck. | I am holding it because that is all I can do.'
'ems-gunshot-wound' = 'It came from the car. I did not see a face. | I felt it before I heard it. That is the strange part. | Is there a lot of blood? Do not lie to me about the blood.'
'ems-head-injury' = 'I do not remember anything after the kerb. | Somebody said I was out for a minute. I do not believe them. | I keep wanting to go to sleep. Tell me I can go to sleep.'
'ems-heat-exhaustion' = 'I have been out in it since the morning. No shade, no water. | I stopped feeling hot a while ago. Now I am cold, which makes no sense. | I am not going to hospital. I just need to sit for a minute.'
'ems-industrial-accident' = 'The guard came off the machine. It should never have been off. | I have been on that line eleven years. Nothing has ever done that. | The foreman is not here. Nobody knows where the foreman is.'
'ems-machinery-shear' = 'It came down on the sleeve and then it was my arm. | It is holding me. I can feel it holding me. | Talk to me. Just keep talking to me.'
'ems-multiple-shooting' = 'We were both outside. It all happened at once. | I got down behind the car. He did not get down in time. | Do not leave him. Whatever else you do, do not leave him.'
'ems-multiple-stabbing' = 'It was three of them and it was quick. | My friend is by the bins. He is worse off than me. | I cannot stand up. Every time I try, it goes.'
'ems-overdose-park' = 'It was meant to be the same as always. It was not the same. | Nobody gave it to me. I am not saying who did. | There is no name on it, is there. There is never a name on it.'
'ems-overdose-teen' = 'It is my friend. She took something at the party. | I do not know what it was. Nobody at that party knows what it was. | Is she awake? Just tell me if she is awake.'
'ems-pedestrian-struck' = 'I was on the crossing. I am sure I was on the crossing. | It came from the left. I only heard it. | Somebody has my bag. My bag is over by the wall.'
'ems-psychiatric' = 'I do not need an ambulance. I am not the one who called. | My brother is inside and he has not come out of that room in three days. | He is not a danger to anybody. He is frightened, that is all.'
'ems-punch-injury' = 'One punch. That is all it was, one punch. | He walked off towards the taxi rank. | My teeth feel loose. Is that normal, teeth feeling loose?'
'ems-respiratory' = 'It came on in the night. I have been sat up since four. | The blue inhaler is finished and the other one makes my heart race. | If I lean forward it is easier. Let me lean forward.'
'ems-seizure' = 'It has happened before. Not like this, but it has happened. | I bit my tongue. I can taste it. | Everybody is staring at me. Can you move them back?'
'ems-sepsis' = 'It started as a chest thing last week. | I have been shaking since the morning and I cannot keep anything down. | Is it the infection? Tell me straight, is it the infection?'
'ems-sport-head' = 'I went up for the ball and I do not remember landing. | How long was I out? Nobody will tell me how long. | I want to go back on. I know what you are going to say.'
'ems-sports-injury' = 'It was the tackle. Studs up, right on the shin. | I heard it crack before I felt anything. | Do not let them carry me off. I can hop, I have done it before.'
'ems-stab-wound' = 'Outside the takeaway. It took two seconds. | I have a jacket over it. Somebody told me to hold the jacket. | Is that much blood normal? Somebody answer me.'
'ems-stairs-fall' = 'I missed the last step with a full basket in my arms. | I went down the whole flight. I remember all of it. | It is my back and my wrist. The wrist took the landing.'
'ems-stroke' = 'It came on while I was on the phone. The words just went. | My face feels wrong on this side. I can feel it drooping. | What time is it? Somebody write down what time it is.'
'ems-withdrawal' = 'Third day. It is always the third day. | I am not going to hospital. They will only do the same thing again. | I have done it before. I can do it again. I just need to get through tonight.'

# ============================================================ Fire
