'fire-caravan' = 'It started inside. Nobody was in it, thank God. | There is a gas bottle under the sink. The big one. | We are all out of ours, but there are four more down that row.'
'fire-car-row' = 'One went up and then it was two, and then it was all of them. | They are parked nose to tail. That is the whole problem. | People are still trying to drive out. Somebody needs to stop them.'
'fire-chimney' = 'It is in the chimney. It has been going since the fire was lit. | The sweep was booked for next month. That is the truth of it. | I have not put water on it. Somebody told me not to.'
'fire-commercial-bins' = 'It is the bins round the back. It has been smouldering all night. | It has taken the fence, and the fence goes to the yard. | The yard is full of pallets. Hundreds of them.'
'fire-electrical-depot' = 'We killed the power at the main. Everybody is out and counted. | It is the cabinet by the loading bay. It has been arcing for a week. | Nobody goes near that bay. I have made sure of that.'
'fire-factory' = 'Everybody is out. We counted them at the gate. | It is in the paint store. That is the one that frightens me. | There is a man unaccounted for. He was on the mezzanine.'
'fire-flat-smoke' = 'The smoke is in the stairwell and it is going up. | Nobody has come past me and I have been here ten minutes. | The door of number six is warm. I am not touching it.'
'fire-garage' = 'There is a motorbike in there and a can of petrol beside it. | It is attached to the house. That is what I am worried about. | I opened the door and it went up in my face. That is why my eyebrows have gone.'
'fire-gas-leak' = 'I can smell it from here. It has been all morning. | The engineers are not coming until tomorrow. I have it in writing. | It is strongest outside number eleven. That is where I would start.'
'fire-grass-fire' = 'It started at the path and the wind has it now. | There are houses behind the ridge. They will not see it until it is on them. | Two of us have been beating it with coats. It is doing nothing.'
'fire-grass-hills' = 'It is going up the hill rather than across. That is something. | If the wind turns it comes down onto the gardens. | Everybody on the top road has been told to leave. Not all of them have.'
'fire-house-occupied' = 'There is somebody in the back bedroom. My brother is in the back bedroom. | I could not get up the stairs. The smoke beat me back. | He is deaf. You need to know that before you go in, he is deaf.'
